  The fake unit's ModelRepo.xml: HAND-WRITTEN for qcsuite's mock, in the shape of
  the real file (Category > Model > Parameter, the same attribute names). It is NOT
  Neural DSP's data: names, parameter lists and wire order mirror the fake catalog
  in fake_data.py (which is synthetic), so every Parameter here sits at the same
  index as in the fake catalog (tests/test_feat_editor.py checks that). The display
  attributes (displayPos, skew, stepNames, min_string, hidden, ...) are invented to
  exercise the editor the way the real file does. Models not listed fall back to the
  catalog order with no extras, as they would if the real fetch failed.
  The tm ("Based on ...") strings are the origins Neural DSP publishes in its device
  list, so the editor's real-gear photo panel can be tried on the mock.
-->
